<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.7.1: Comparing Graphs of Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01848</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.7.1: Comparing Graphs of Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>3f9f4396-948d-48b6-8179-110d9f7bf082</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Which one doesn’t belong?</para>

    
    <div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-between">
      <div class="os-raise-mx-auto">
        <para>Graph A</para>
        <para><figure><media alt="Graph of a line, origin O, with grid. Horizontal axis from negative 2 to 2 by 1’s. Vertical axis from negative 2 to 6 by ones. Line passes through negative 2 comma 2, 0 comma 2, and 2 comma 2.&quot; height=&quot;200"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3264a00e3d1c43ca84640c08ef7fa87c84d921c0"/></media></figure></para>
      </div>
      <div class="os-raise-mx-auto"> 
        <para>Graph B</para>
         <para><figure><media alt="Graph of a line, origin O, with grid. Horizontal axis from negative 2 to 2 by 1’s. Vertical axis from negative 2 to 6 by ones. Line passes through negative 1 comma negative 2, 0 comma 2, and 1 comma 6.&quot; height=&quot;200"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/cb0ec9c517438e5532657c3a39c4431dc1d178a3"/></media></figure></para>
       </div>
    </div>
    <div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-between">
      <div class="os-raise-mx-auto">
        <para>Graph C</para>
        <para><figure><media alt="Graph of 13 data points."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2dedbe2887024dd94f014270367df3daa0c81126"/></media></figure></para>
      </div>
      <div class="os-raise-mx-auto"> 
        <para>Graph D</para>
        <para><figure><media alt="Graph of curved line, origin O, with grid. Horizontal axis from negative 2 to 2 by 1’s. Vertical axis from negative 2 to 6 by 1’s. Line passes through negative 1 comma point 5, 0 comma 3 point 5, 1 comma 7.&quot; height=&quot;200"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f7257dbf2a252a44bd485dee393962deb81e3e3f"/></media></figure></para>
       </div>
    </div>

  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Graph A is the only graph where the \(y\)-values don’t change.</para>
    <para>Graph B is the only graph where the \(y\)-value increases by a constant rate.</para>
    <para>Graph C is the only graph that is not continuous.</para>
    <para>Graph D is the only graph that does not intersect the \(y\)-axis at \(2\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
